{
  "_comment": "Canonical inventory of EVERY OpenTelemetry instrument this repository declares, and the Prometheus series each one actually exports. Generated from the source tree and verified against a real /metrics scrape; MetricNameContractTests keeps both ends honest. Companion to observability/slo-metric-contract.json, which covers the narrower cross-repo SLO surface (honua-server#3322, honua-release#5).",
  "_why": "The OpenTelemetry Prometheus exporter derives the exported series name from the instrument name AND its `unit`: it maps the unit through the UCUM table and appends it when the name does not already end in the mapped form. So `honua.alerts.dispatch_backlog_count` with unit \"dispatches\" was exported as `honua_alerts_dispatch_backlog_count_dispatches`, and `honua_serving_request_duration_ms` with unit \"ms\" as `honua_serving_request_duration_ms_milliseconds_count`. Nothing breaks at build time: a PromQL query against the absent name returns an EMPTY VECTOR, so `rate()` yields nothing, a ratio over it yields nothing, the panel renders blank and the alert never fires. The failure mode is silence, not noise, which is why this file and its guard exist (honua-server#3323).",
  "_rules": "1. `series` is the Prometheus text-exposition name, NOT the .NET instrument name. 2. Dots and dashes in an instrument name are sanitized to underscores by the exporter. 3. A Counter/ObservableCounter gains a `_total` suffix unless its name already ends in `_total`. 4. A Histogram emits only `_bucket`/`_count`/`_sum` children, never its bare base name. 5. Gauges and UpDownCounters export under the sanitized name unchanged. 6. A `unit` is only safe when the exporter would append nothing: an annotation unit in braces (`{state}`, `{call}`) is dropped entirely, and a unit whose UCUM form the name already ends with (`bytes`, `seconds`, `percent`, `ratio`) is not repeated. Any other unit RENAMES the series. Prefer `unit: null` and carry the unit in the instrument name and description.",
  "_maintenance": "Do not hand-edit for convenience. If MetricNameContractTests fails, either the source or this file is wrong: fix whichever one diverged from the name consumers query. Adding an instrument means adding an entry here; changing a unit means the exported series name changed and every dashboard, alert rule and runbook naming it must change with it.",
  "version": 1,
  "label_names": {
    "_comment": "Prometheus LABEL names that begin with `honua_` and therefore look like series names to a naive scan. They are instrument tag keys sanitized by the exporter (honua.protocol -> honua_protocol), not metrics.",
    "names": [
      "honua_protocol",
      "honua_operation",
      "honua_controlplane_target_kind",
      "honua_controlplane_backend",
      "honua_controlplane_execution_kind",
      "honua_controlplane_execution_status",
      "honua_controlplane_execution_reconcile_outcome"
    ]
  },
  "not_emitted": [
    {
      "series": "honua_rate_limit_violations_total",
      "referenced_by": "docs/guides/deploy/examples/prometheus-alerts.yml (HonuaRateLimitViolationsHigh)",
      "reason": "No component declares this instrument. The rate limiter records no counter, so the rule is inert. Listed so the consumer guard treats it as a KNOWN gap rather than accepting any unknown name -- a typo in a real metric name still fails."
    },
    {
      "series": "honua_circuit_breaker_state_changes_total",
      "referenced_by": "docs/guides/deploy/examples/prometheus-alerts.yml (HonuaCircuitBreakerOpen)",
      "reason": "No component declares this instrument. Resilience circuit-breaker state is surfaced through health-check data, not a metric."
    },
    {
      "series": "honua_span_duration_ms_bucket",
      "referenced_by": "docker/monitoring/grafana/dashboards/honua-slow-traces.json",
      "reason": "The dashboard is explicitly a placeholder: it needs a per-ActivitySource span-duration histogram that no meter declares. Its panels render blank today."
    },
    {
      "series": "honua_span_duration_ms_count",
      "referenced_by": "docker/monitoring/grafana/dashboards/honua-slow-traces.json",
      "reason": "As honua_span_duration_ms_bucket."
    }
  ],
